{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/a1-grammar-build-a-sentence/audio/main-cff3dd9646f7.mp3","durationSec":171.144,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":1.18,"text":"You meet Emma and Ben."},{"start":1.18,"end":3.9,"text":"Be tells a name, job, place or feeling."},{"start":4.46,"end":6.24,"text":"Person, Be, Short form."},{"start":6.7,"end":7.8,"text":"I, am, I'm."},{"start":8.02,"end":10.54,"text":"he, she, it, is, he's, she's, it's."},{"start":10.78,"end":13.9,"text":"you, we, they, are, you're, we're, they're."},{"start":13.9,"end":16.06,"text":"Rule: Match am, is or are to the person."},{"start":16.62,"end":18.76,"text":"For a yes/no question, put be first."},{"start":19.34,"end":21.76,"text":"For a negative, add not after be."},{"start":21.76,"end":23.86,"text":"The word you can mean one person or a group."},{"start":24.16,"end":25.84,"text":"Use it for weather and time: It's sunny."},{"start":26.18,"end":27.5,"text":"It's three o'clock."},{"start":27.5,"end":29.6,"text":"Statement: Ben is at school."},{"start":30.14,"end":31.6,"text":"Question: Is Ben at school?"},{"start":32.06,"end":32.86,"text":"Yes, he is."},{"start":33.66,"end":34.5,"text":"/ No, he isn't."},{"start":34.5,"end":36.42,"text":"Negative: Ben is not at school."},{"start":36.72,"end":37.22,"text":"Emma is a teacher."},{"start":37.6,"end":38.24,"text":"Is she a teacher?"},{"start":38.8,"end":39.52,"text":"Yes, she is."},{"start":39.88,"end":40.66,"text":"/ No, she isn't."},{"start":41.08,"end":41.88,"text":"They are at home."},{"start":42.54,"end":43.2,"text":"Are they at home?"},{"start":43.62,"end":44.32,"text":"Yes, they are."},{"start":44.78,"end":45.5,"text":"/ No, they aren't."},{"start":46.36,"end":47.28,"text":"Ben, are you ready?"},{"start":47.7,"end":48.34,"text":"Yes, I am."},{"start":48.66,"end":49.18,"text":"/ No, I'm not."},{"start":49.76,"end":50.66,"text":"Class, are you ready?"},{"start":51.14,"end":51.8,"text":"Yes, we are."},{"start":52.22,"end":53.94,"text":"Watch out: Not Do you are ready?"},{"start":54.34,"end":55.48,"text":"Say Are you ready?"},{"start":56.26,"end":58,"text":"Ben and Emma talk in class."},{"start":58,"end":60.4,"text":"Person or thing, Verb, Other words."},{"start":60.9,"end":61.56,"text":"We, read, –."},{"start":62.04,"end":63.38,"text":"We, read, books at home."},{"start":63.82,"end":64.8,"text":"He, is, happy."},{"start":64.8,"end":68.9,"text":"Rule: In a statement, the person or thing comes before the verb."},{"start":69.3,"end":72.02,"text":"A question word comes first, before be."},{"start":72.02,"end":73.12,"text":"Where asks about a place."},{"start":73.64,"end":74.72,"text":"What asks about a thing."},{"start":75.22,"end":75.68,"text":"We read."},{"start":76.06,"end":76.8,"text":"We = subject."},{"start":77.26,"end":78.04,"text":"Read = verb."},{"start":78.38,"end":79.38,"text":"It is a complete sentence."},{"start":79.98,"end":80.6,"text":"They play football."},{"start":81.04,"end":81.74,"text":"They = subject."},{"start":82.3,"end":83,"text":"Play = verb."},{"start":83.5,"end":84.08,"text":"He is happy."},{"start":84.08,"end":85.54,"text":"This sentence needs happy."},{"start":86.08,"end":86.98,"text":"We read books at home."},{"start":86.98,"end":88.72,"text":"You can add these words."},{"start":89.2,"end":89.78,"text":"Where is the bag?"},{"start":90,"end":90.58,"text":"It's on the chair."},{"start":91.02,"end":91.7,"text":"/ What is your name?"},{"start":92.16,"end":92.84,"text":"My name is Ben."},{"start":93.66,"end":95.34,"text":"Watch out: Not Where the bag is?"},{"start":95.9,"end":97,"text":"Say Where is the bag?"},{"start":97,"end":99.94,"text":"Study: Compare Emma is at school."},{"start":100.44,"end":101.7,"text":"and Is Emma at school?"},{"start":102.18,"end":102.62,"text":"What changes?"},{"start":103.44,"end":104.24,"text":"Ben is at the door."},{"start":104.24,"end":106.5,"text":"Be tells a feeling or a place."},{"start":107.08,"end":109.36,"text":"An action verb shows an action, like walk."},{"start":109.36,"end":110.98,"text":"Be, Action verb."},{"start":111.74,"end":113.22,"text":"I am ready, I walk to school."},{"start":113.64,"end":115.64,"text":"They are at home, They read books."},{"start":115.64,"end":119.54,"text":"Rule: Never put be just before a verb like go."},{"start":120.36,"end":121.08,"text":"I am happy."},{"start":121.6,"end":122.4,"text":"She is tired."},{"start":122.9,"end":124.24,"text":"We play football after school."},{"start":124.72,"end":125.62,"text":"They read at home."},{"start":126.36,"end":129.04,"text":"Watch out: Not I am go to school."},{"start":129.78,"end":130.56,"text":"Go is the verb."},{"start":131.18,"end":132.1,"text":"Am is extra."},{"start":132.66,"end":133.7,"text":"Say I go to school."},{"start":133.7,"end":135.58,"text":"Emma writes on the board."},{"start":136.56,"end":139.28,"text":"A capital letter is a big letter, like A."},{"start":140,"end":141.6,"text":"Sentence, Example."},{"start":142.54,"end":144.12,"text":"statement, We are here."},{"start":144.98,"end":146.88,"text":"question, Are we here."},{"start":148.32,"end":150.28,"text":"Rule: Start with a capital letter."},{"start":150.62,"end":152.62,"text":"End with a full stop or question mark."},{"start":153.66,"end":155.96,"text":"I and names always have a capital letter."},{"start":156.68,"end":159.48,"text":"Put one space between words: I am here."},{"start":160.22,"end":160.84,"text":"I am ready."},{"start":160.84,"end":162.88,"text":"Ben and I read."},{"start":163.72,"end":164.36,"text":"Where is Ben?"},{"start":165.04,"end":165.72,"text":"Are you happy?"},{"start":166.5,"end":168.9,"text":"Watch out: Not are you ready."},{"start":169.46,"end":170.62,"text":"Say Are you ready?"}],"words":[{"text":"You","start":0,"end":0.18},{"text":"meet","start":0.18,"end":0.38},{"text":"Emma","start":0.38,"end":0.7},{"text":"and","start":0.7,"end":0.96},{"text":"Ben","start":0.96,"end":1.18},{"text":"Be","start":1.18,"end":1.86},{"